    "subdials": {
      "radiusFactor": 1.0,
      "_comment": "Scales the SOLVED shared sub-dial radius (small seconds + reserve). Applied in solveLayout, so it needs a reload; TODO 33's boot assert guards the wells against the dial's CENTRE BORE, so an oversized factor warns rather than silently colliding. Position stays a non-knob of THIS layer and is a dimension of the SPEC (§94: ?d4= moves the seconds station, ?rsvr= the reserve station) — finish scales the solved radius and never places a well. BOUNDS: max 1.0 because the solved radius already sits on the ceiling. That ceiling MOVED: it used to be §25 C's (well ring vs the central setting wheel, wellR 10.20) and the note here read 'factor 1.15 penetrates by 1.33' — measured before TODO 26 gave the dial thickness and lifted the wells out of the setting lane, which retired that wall. What binds now is the centre bore (3.20 + 0.2 wall + 0.15 margin), so the solve grew 10.20 → 11.85 and 1.0 is again exactly the ceiling; measured, factor 1.02 already goes NEGATIVE on the reserve well (web -0.09 against the required 0.15) and leaves 0.01 on the seconds. Min 0.5 because below half size the wells swallow their own hands.",
      "_bounds": {
        "radiusFactor": [
          0.5,
          1.0
        ]
      },
      "_labels": {
        "radiusFactor": "Sub-dial size"
      }
    }
  },
